.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Catalogue size cap (decision 4 refined):** pairwise joint moves are restricted to the top-K = 10 users by nominal unilateral surplus **and their top-2 legal options each** (≤ 45 × 4 = 180 rows); unilateral rows ≤ users × legal options (≈ 2 700); evacuation sets ≤ active beams (≈ 40); S0 proposals ≤ 200. Catalogue ≤ ≈ 3 200 rows per anchor.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **C3-SET-REPRESENTATION** — set head input = permutation-invariant pooling (sum and max) over the changed users' per-user vectors (their Q1 row for the selected action, their incumbent row, `missing_incumbent`), concatenated with global resource context per affected beam (occupancy before/after, activation change, interference summary, cap margin), padded to |A| ≤ 4 with masks; a two-layer MLP on the pooled vector; anchored zeros by construction (output × 𝟙[|A| ≥ 2]). Shapley for reporting: exact over subsets for |A| ≤ 4.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **LEARNER-SEED-VALUES** — twelve learner seeds derived from domains `V025_LEARNER/seed/{1..12}` by the repository seed rule (no hand-picked integers); the external BASELINE's implementation sha256 is recorded in the allocation manifest.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGEC-SPEC-2026-09-08.md:15:11. **ZERO-BIT-DISPOSITION** — contract v1 §D3. **ZERO-QOS-BASELINE** — if the DROP arm's event count is zero and FULL's is positive, the relative handover/Φ margin fails by rule (`FAIL_UNDEFINED_DENOMINATOR`); if both are zero, non-inferior by rule; recorded per contrast.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:8:4. **Catalogue census** — **CHANGE** for real worlds: the complete Cartesian product of legal assignments is used only when it has ≤ 4 096 configurations (synthetic worlds). Otherwise the union catalogue is the bounded set: (i) every unilateral move of every user to every legal option; (ii) the S0 deployable proposals (top-two per user) and all frozen beam evacuations; (iii) all pairwise joint moves among the top-K = 10 users ranked by nominal unilateral surplus, over all their legal option pairs; (iv) per-active-beam evacuation sets (every user of the beam to its best legal alternative). J1 = the best changed-user-count > 1 configuration in this catalogue; U1 = the best in (i). The catalogue definition and its digest are sealed; the per-world superset check of stage-3 item 10 reports how many legal options fall outside the shortlist.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **LC-SRS e_i binding** — **CHANGE**: under the sealed whole-network C1 (which already contains every unilateral bit and joule change of the network), the unilateral externality e_i is inside C1, so the successor C3 target carries **no e_i term**: z₃,ᵢ = Ψ/2 for pairs and the equal-share (Shapley) split of the set interaction for larger sets, with Ψ computed on F = B − η_ref·E per regime (per-cell re-optimisation). This is the round-6 no-double-counting rule; the historical LC-SRS e_i (defined for an own-bits-only C1) is not transferred.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **QoS guard margins** — **CHANGE** (numeric, prospective): FULL is QoS non-inferior to a DROP arm when the 95 % cluster-bootstrap interval of (FULL − DROP) lies above −0.5 pp for complete-service availability, and the interval of the relative change lies below +5 % for both the handover rate and the Φ-priced handover cost per user-step. Catalogue/service exclusion thresholds do not exclude configurations; they score and report (the service guard used by the deployable decoder is the sealed one from C3-S: no served-count decrease versus the BASE proposal).
