.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **B2 — factor arms cannot measure component marginals (design CHANGE).** The set decoder's score for FULL/DROP arms is the **sum of the declared targets**, not the exact realised objective: S(config) = C1(config) + C2(config) + C3(config), each the declared target in bits computed by the oracle from the same nominal physics (C1 whole-network difference surplus + Φ; C2 three-offset forecasts with −κ; C3 = interaction share per decision item 5 / Shapley for sets). DROP_Cx removes exactly one term inside the **same selector class and the same catalogue**; `DROP_C3` = no interaction term (joint search kept); an additional `UNI` arm = unilateral-only search with all three terms is reported separately (search value ≠ interaction value); `S_UNI` (stage-4 item 11) is the iterated exact-unilateral comparator. The exact-F oracle is a **ceiling arm** (U1/J1/union certificates), never a factor arm. Marginals are measured on the realised pooled endpoint ΣB/ΣE, never on nominal scores. KATs: on a synthetic world with a constructed non-zero interaction, FULL and DROP_C3 select different configurations and the realised marginal equals the hand-computed value; with zero interaction they coincide; DROP_C1/DROP_C2 differ from FULL on fixtures where the dropped term is decisive.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:8:3. **Uncertainty reporting.** The primary uncertainty statement for every contrast is a **cluster bootstrap that recomputes ΣB/ΣE per resample** (clusters = TLE dates × training seeds as declared in the evaluation design); paired per-world log-EE intervals are supplementary and are never substituted for the pooled-ratio interval.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Claim wording.** The success claim is conditional and intersection–union: "with the other two components enabled, each of the three FULL − DROP pooled-EE contrasts exceeds its prespecified margin δ = +0.5 pp with the 95 % lower bound above it, and FULL is QoS non-inferior to each DROP"; the all-neutral cell supports the FULL − ALL_NEUTRAL comparison; main effects across all backgrounds are not claimed without the full 2³ factorial.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.4-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **δ units.** The success margin is a **relative** pooled-EE gain: EE_FULL / EE_DROP − 1 ≥ +0.5 % (the phrase "+0.5 pp" in v1.2 §4 meant this relative percentage; pooled EE has no percentage-point scale). The 95 % lower bound of that relative gain must exceed +0.5 %.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.4-ERRATUM-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Interval convention.** All bootstrap intervals are central 95 % percentile intervals (2.5th/97.5th percentiles, linear interpolation as implemented by `numpy.quantile` default); the one-sided decision uses the corresponding endpoint (2.5th for gains and availability, 97.5th for handover rate and Φ-priced cost), which is conservative relative to a 5 % one-sided bound and is retained as declared.
