    17	## Canonical ordering and truncation
    18	
    19	- The complete serialized relation block is sorted by `(source beam key,
    20	  target beam key)`. Construction also canonicalizes the in-memory tuple, so
    21	  caller order cannot affect payload bytes, payload hashes, or predictions.
    22	- The encoder limit is **K = 32 directed pairs**.
    23	- Selection is top-K by descending absolute gain. Ties are resolved by source
    24	  beam key and then target beam key. The selected rows are put back into
    25	  canonical `(source, target)` order before encoding.
    26	- Each of the 32 positions carries normalized deterministic source-key hash,
    27	  normalized deterministic target-key hash, gain, and a presence bit. Missing
    28	  positions are zero-padded. The `math.fsum` of every omitted gain is appended
    29	  as a residual, making the block width 129 and preventing silent loss.
    30	- The payload retains the complete canonical relation list and declares K and
    31	  the residual sum. The 180 existing pilot shards contain 2, 6, or 12 pairs,
    32	  so none would be truncated and every residual is zero.
