+| C1+C2 | +106.501 | -116.073 | +222.573 | 254.947 | 282.348 | 8/10 |
+
+[EXEC] The equal C2 bias and MAE mean every C2 error in these ten cases was upward; this is a sign/bias failure, not only a scale mismatch. The C1 errors have mixed signs and large magnitude; they are not explained by one multiplicative calibration. Inputs and implementations are the same as for the preceding table. [INFERENCE] Most of the missing cancellation comes from C2: the current exact C2 is strongly negative at four anchors while the learned C2 is positive or near zero.
+
+### Coalition-size diagnostic
+
+[EXEC] To separate size from catalogue selection, I took the canonical first `k` changed users (user-id order) from each saved size-100 profile and summed their exact unilateral C1/C2 values and learned scores. Sizes 1–6 below are controlled prefixes, not the actual catalogue winner at that size. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-min-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/evaluation/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-raw-receipts.jsonl:1`; `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:154-173`, `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:251-310`; `src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:627-645`)
+
