+| 100 | +34.990 | +15.962 | -19.028 | -151.063 | +90.539 | +241.602 | -116.073 | +106.501 | +222.573 | 8 |
+
+[INFERENCE] The error grows with accumulated users, but it is present at size one: the wrong object is being learned before coalition interaction enters. The size-100 symptom is amplification of a singleton/additive error, not evidence that C3 caused it.
+
+### Conflict with the previously reported “exact additive” receipt
+
+[EXEC] The raw receipt stores `exact_additive_score` values of `+1017.570`, `-2260.609`, `-1327.986`, `+5428.338`, and `-456.749` by anchor, whereas current-source exact C1 replay gives `+41.647`, `+119.148`, `+12.242`, `-111.203`, and `+113.116`. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-min-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/evaluation/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-raw-receipts.jsonl:1`; exact-additive helper at `scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1328-1380`)
+
+[READ] That receipt's helper computes immediate exact C1 plus the preference term; it does not persist a separate exact C2. (`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1328-1380`) [EXEC] The saved source artifact and current tree have the same physics digest but not the same code digest. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/source/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-source-anchor-000.jsonl:2`; `artifacts/v025-pilot-min-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/evaluation/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-raw-receipts.jsonl:1`) [INFERENCE] The large stored cancellation cannot be treated as reproducible current ground truth; adapter/code drift or a receipt-generation defect remains unresolved. This does not rescue the learned path: the current evaluator replay independently shows the sign and magnitude failures above.
+
+## 2. Acceptance tests, one by one
+
+### Contract T1 — `test_T1_exhaustive_decomposition_and_intervention`
+
+[READ] **Named obligation:** a hand-computed three-user fixture must exercise additive/synergistic/antagonistic cases, a dummy user, nonzero preference, a future outage, production target construction and selectors, exact identities, oracle DROP behavior, neutral-source retention/training, and deployment knockout. (`V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:42-44`)
+
+[READ] **What it actually rejects:** wrong algebra in the target identities and lost-offset handling (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:353-436`); wrong row/head shapes (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:444-452`); a selector that ignores an injected C3 score (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:453-485`); and a knockout that fails to remove manually installed one-hot C1/C2 contributions (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:487-521`).
+
+[READ] **Specific wrong C1/C2 implementation it does not reject:** the production fallback that substitutes link-ratio proxy labels for exact whole-network C1/C2. The fixture constructs `NetworkOutcome` values and coalition rows by hand, then hand-edits head inputs and weights; it never passes pilot C1/C2 source generation through the exact evaluator and compares the resulting labels. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:97-107`, `tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:176-217`, `tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:487-521`; proxy at `scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:403-462`) [READ] Its neutral-source assertion is specific to DROP_C3, not C1 or C2. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:523-546`) **For wrong learned C1/C2 target generation, the answer is: none.** [INFERENCE] A fixture that labels its own cases and then recovers those labels is an algebra KAT, not evidence that the production labels represent the physics.
+
+### Contract T2 — `test_T2_information_twins_reversal_and_additive_placebo`
+
+[READ] **Named obligation:** identical per-user rows with opposite joint interactions must be separated by full coalition context and become ambiguous without cross-gains; hidden/post-decision information must not affect actions; identities, repair, timeout/fallback, and an additive placebo must be exercised through production paths. (`V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:44`; `V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5-7`)
+
+[READ] **What it actually rejects:** certain post-decision/hidden-state leaks in extracted features (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:732-765`), mismatched interface behavior (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:817-840`), infeasible-profile repair/fallback errors (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:842-891`), and failure to fit its constructed additive placebo (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:893-921`).
+
+[READ] **Specific wrong C1/C2 implementation it rejects:** none for exact-label fidelity. It does not compare production C1/C2 labels or predictions with exact evaluator singletons. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:647-921`) [INFERENCE] Its relevance to C1/C2 is limited to interface/leakage properties; passing it cannot exclude the proxy-label defect or the collisions in section 3.
+
+### Contract T3 — `test_T3_crossed_cluster_real_merger_coverage_and_power`
+
+[READ] **Named obligation:** validate crossed date/seed/world inference, pooled ratios, zero/undefined cells, injected alternatives, conjunction behavior, coverage, power, and QoS rejection through the real merger. (`V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:45`; `V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:8`)
+
+[READ] **What it actually rejects:** merger, aggregation, interval, conjunction, and power-calibration defects under its synthetic receipt model. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:983-1179`) [READ] The fixture evaluator hard-codes outcome bits and energies by arm rather than invoking real C1/C2 scoring. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:924-951`) **For a wrong C1/C2 scorer or ablation, the answer is: none.**
+
+### Supporting Stage-C tests that touch C1/C2
+
+| test | stated/visible obligation | specific wrong implementation rejected | important blind spot |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `test_synthetic_end_to_end_twelve_seeds_six_arms` | [READ] Pipeline can run and emit expected inventory/report fields. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:63-99`) | [READ] Missing arms, malformed artifacts, or gross pipeline wiring. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:63-99`) | [READ] No exact C1/C2 comparison; synthetic labels are assigned directly. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/synthetic.py:123-187`) |
+| `test_golden_tape_to_row_all_q1_q2_fields_and_authorities` | [READ] Q1/Q2 schema and authority extraction on a golden synthetic tape. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:102-166`) | [READ] Missing, reordered, or incorrectly sourced row fields on that fixture. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:102-166`) | [READ] It does not establish sufficiency or exact-label fidelity; labels are synthetic constants/functions. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/synthetic.py:123-187`) |
+| `test_two_user_independent_argmax_cannot_commit_jointly_infeasible_profile` | [READ] Joint validation/repair blocks an infeasible combination of individually attractive actions. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:270-316`) | [READ] A deployer that commits an invalid joint argmax. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:270-316`) | [READ] It does not test score correctness. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:270-316`) |
+| `test_drop_arms_retain_and_update_all_heads` | [READ] DROP heads remain present and update under neutral batches. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:364-388`) | [READ] Removing/freezing heads or mapping DROP_C1 to the informative source. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:364-388`) | [READ] It does not assert DROP_C2's source mapping or any decision difference. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:364-388`) |
+| `test_shard_boundary_recomputes_dimensions_masks_and_labels` | [READ] Shard-boundary authentication recomputes dimensions, masks, and selected fields. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:469-482`) | [READ] Mutation of Q1, mask, lambda, or C1 label in its cases. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:469-482`) | [READ] No C2-label mutation case is present. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_stagec_pipeline.py:469-482`) |
+
+[EXEC] A static AST/path scan found 60 tests in six `tests/physics_v025` files that load implementation files by `spec_from_file_location` from `.scratch`, rather than importing the installed package path; one explicit loader is at `tests/physics_v025/test_stage2_runner.py:11-20`. [READ] The pilot runner likewise dynamically loads the scratch engine and probe. (`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:69-105`) [INFERENCE] Those tests may validate the intended frozen scratch implementation, but they are not package-under-test evidence for `src/mcrl` and should not be counted as such.
+
+## 3. Feature sufficiency
+
+### Encoder audit
+
+[READ] Q1 is a 16-scalar vector and Q2 is a 22-scalar vector. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:29-46`, `src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:48-86`) [READ] The encoders retain focal-action summaries, occupancy/activity summaries, history flags, and a few offset summaries, then normalize them. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:396-481`) [READ] The learner routes only those vectors to the C1/C2 heads; it does not pass action identity, the background association graph, per-interferer cross-gains, a coupled-power solution, or full projected `NetworkOutcome` objects to either head. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:167-172`, `src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:187-260`)
+
+[READ] This is the same class of compression defect found in C3: a structured whole-network quantity is reduced to aggregates before the head sees it. The exact C1 answer depends on whole-network bits, joules, and preference, while exact C2 depends on complete future projected outcomes. (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:130-209`, `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:251-310`) [INFERENCE] No deterministic function of Q1/Q2 alone can be exact over all physically admissible states if those hidden network outcomes can vary while the vectors stay fixed.
+
+### Constructed collision
+
+[EXEC] I constructed two distinct physical actions, `(satellite_id=1, beam_id=1)` and `(satellite_id=2, beam_id=2)`, with identical legal focal summaries and identical Q1/Q2 forecast summaries. In state A, production target helpers returned exact C1 `+100` and C2 `+300`; in state B they returned exact C1 `-10` and C2 `-30`. Production `extract_source_rows` mapped both states to byte-for-byte identical Q1 vectors and identical Q2 vectors. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:396-481`; target computation at `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:154-173`, `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:251-310`; physical action/outcome structures at `src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:176-209`)
+
+[INFERENCE] This is a decisive interface-level collision: physically distinct states with different correct signs can be indistinguishable to both heads. [INFERENCE] The fixture uses valid synthetic `NetworkOutcome` objects; it proves insufficiency of the declared function interface, but it does not claim that the current V025 simulator naturally emits this exact numeric twin.
+
+[EXEC] In the 176,223 production rows, 938 exact Q1-vector keys and 100 exact Q2-vector keys were shared by multiple physical action identities; no exact-vector key had differing proxy labels. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/source/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-source-anchor-000.jsonl:2`; all sibling source shards named by `artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-rows-manifest.json:1`) [INFERENCE] The absence of differing labels is expected, not exculpatory: the fallback labels are themselves functions of the compressed/local primitives, so the corpus cannot expose distinctions its label generator discarded.
+
+## 4. Estimator matching across arms
+
+### Learned neutral-source arms
+
+[READ] The sealed estimand requires identical machinery with only the named route's informative source replaced by its neutral source. (`V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:18-25`) [READ] `SOURCE_MAP` maps FULL to all informative routes, DROP_C1 only to neutral C1, DROP_C2 only to neutral C2, and DROP_C3 only to neutral C3. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:30-35`) [READ] Initialization is cloned across arms and routing selects the named source without removing heads. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:994-1038`) [READ] Neutral batches preserve the input states and replace the target with zero. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:146-164`)
+
+[EXEC] Checkpoint tensors at epoch 200 across all four saved seeds have the intended isolation: DROP_C1 differs from FULL in C1 and is byte-identical in C2/C3; DROP_C2 differs in C2 and is byte-identical in C1/C3. (`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:994-1038`; checkpoint lineage under `artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/checkpoints/`)
+
+[EXEC] A production-row choice fixture over 500 user-anchor contexts from the first five shards produced these FULL-versus-DROP disagreements: seed `925030429265975792`, C1 `0`, C2 `427`; seed `5166716249291843642`, C1 `0`, C2 `0`; seed `6407676579069309528`, C1 `4`, C2 `299`; seed `7234013715671416945`, C1 `2`, C2 `346`. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-rows-manifest.json:1`; scoring/routing at `scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1524-1557`) [INFERENCE] Fixtures therefore exist that make each named ablation disagree with FULL, but C1 has extremely low decision pivotality and one seed makes neither ablation disagree on this sample.
+
+[READ] The minimal realised evaluation did not run DROP_C1 or DROP_C2; both are recorded as skipped. (`V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:90-92`, `V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:109-114`) [INFERENCE] There is checkpoint-level and source-fixture evidence of isolated intervention, but no realised pooled-EE evidence for either C1 or C2 arm in this pilot.
+
+### Exact factor arms and the “all marginals zero” failure class
+
+[READ] The current exact factor scorer explicitly sums only the requested factor targets and does not replace them with the full exact objective; DROP_C1 and DROP_C2 omit different terms. (`.scratch/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:1800-1811`) [READ] The factor-arm selections invoke those distinct factor sets. (`.scratch/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:2733-2736`) [INFERENCE] The known defect in which every DROP arm silently receives FULL's exact objective is not present in this code path.
+
+[READ] The acceptance fixtures hand-construct factor values, so they prove arithmetic separation but not that real exact C1/C2 factors are nonzero and decision-relevant. (`tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:176-217`, `tests/stagec_v025/test_contract_v1_acceptance.py:353-436`) [EXEC] The production-row choice replay above supplies the missing disagreement fixture for the learned arms, although only rarely for C1.
+
+## 5. Corpus coverage
+
+[EXEC] Streaming all 180 source shards produced the following inventory. The manifest records 87,997 rows for world 1 and 88,226 for world 2, totaling 176,223. (`artifacts/v025-pilot-c3-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/PILOT_NOT_CLAIM-rows-manifest.json:1`)
